      "kind": "ability",
      "name": "Silencing Stab",
      "actions": "reaction",
      "category": "defensive",
      "text": "Trigger A creature within the enfiron's reach speaks\n\n---\nEffect The enfiron makes a spike Strike against the triggering creature. If the enfiron is under the effects of Change Shape, the Strike deals piercing damage regardless of their appearance. If the target fails the saving throw against enfiron venom, it's afflicted at stage 2. The enfiron also attempts a Deception check, comparing the result to the Perception DCs of all creatures that can see the attack (excluding the target). On a success, that creature is unaware of the attack."
    },
    {
      "kind": "ability",
      "name": "Change Shape",
      "actions": 1,
      "category": "offensive",
      "traits": [
        "concentrate",
        "divine",
        "polymorph"
      ],
      "text": "The enfiron can take the appearance of any Small or Medium humanoid. This doesn't change their Speed or their attack and damage modifiers with their Strikes but might change the damage type their Strikes deal (typically to bludgeoning).\n\n---"
    },
    {
      "kind": "ability",
      "name": "Enfiron Venom",
      "category": "offensive",
      "traits": [
        "poison"
      ],
      "text": "Saving Throw DC 34 Fortitude save\n\nMaximum Duration 6 rounds\n\nStage 1 6d6 poison damage and Stupefied 1 (1 round)\n\nStage 2 7d6 poison damage, Stupefied 2, and unable to speak (1 round)\n\nStage 3 8d6 poison damage, stupefied 2, unable to speak, and must hold its breath or suffocate (1 round)"
    },
    {
      "kind": "ability",
      "name": "Hidden Wounds",
      "category": "offensive",
      "traits": [
        "divine",
        "illusion"
      ],
      "text": "Any wounds the enfiron inflicts, even from spells, appear to be instantly but superficially mended, as if no violence took place against the target. A creature attempting to Treat Wounds on a victim must first disbelieve the illusion (DC 31 Perception check check) or take a –2 circumstance penalty to the check. If a creature fails a check to Treat Wounds without first disbelieving the illusion, they get a critical failure instead."
    },
